# TIER 1 - eigenvalue-following saddle refinement from a CONVERGED NEB climbing image
# Phase B Round 4: start from the harvested band CI geometry, with an exact
# initial Hessian (Calc_Hess true). FREQ in the same job gives the mode audit.
# Run ONE job at a time on the local laptop; MPI spawn is blocked in this
# environment, so nprocs stays at 1.
# Launch only through cmd, never PowerShell:
#   cmd /c "D:\ORCA_6.1.0\orca.exe optts_bandX_ci.inp > optts_bandX_ci.out"

! XTB2 OPTTS FREQ

%geom
  Calc_Hess true
  MaxIter 300
end

%pal nprocs 1 end

* xyzfile 0 1 neb_ts_bandX_NEB-CI_converged.xyz

# After ORCA TERMINATED NORMALLY:
#   1) A2 mode audit on the FREQ block in this same output file;
#   2) displace the refined saddle +-0.01 nm along the single reactive
#      imaginary mode and optimize both directions (! XTB2 OPT FREQ);
#   3) both directions must land on the two intended canonical minima
#      (energy within 5 kJ/mol; for band D also confirm endpoints by geometry);
#   4) only then may the barrier enter the register as Accepted.
